# The participant's Python environment, ~/venv (build.sh step 4; issue #474). Compiled, with
# hashes, into venv-requirements.txt, which build.sh installs with --require-hashes:
#   cd workshop/ami/files && uv pip compile -q --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_39 --exclude-newer 2026-10-17T00:00:00Z \
#     --exclude-newer-package certifi=2026-10-24T00:00:00Z \
#     --generate-hashes venv-requirements.in -o venv-requirements.txt
# certifi has a later cutoff than the rest, for 2026.10.23, whose cacert.pem has no emSign ECC
# Root CA - G3 (#671). Move certifi with uv.lock's (tests/workshop/test_trust_stores.py).
# PyX, the one sdist, builds with setuptools from venv-build-constraints.txt (hashes, same pin).
# The image's first five, unpinned until issue #474:
numpy
sympy
matplotlib
jupyter
cypari2
# Numerics, data, graphs and statistics:
scipy
pandas
networkx
statsmodels
scikit-learn
seaborn
# Optimization: HiGHS, SCIP, PuLP (with CBC), CVXPY, OR-Tools. PuLP 4.0 (Sep 25, 2026) dropped
# the bundled CBC and the `LpVariable("x", lowBound=0)` constructor that most PuLP code uses:
# 3.x keeps both.
highspy
pyscipopt
pulp<4
cvxpy
ortools
# Low-dimensional topology (both run headless):
snappy
regina
